258
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:41,080
I came here with that guy.

259
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:43,960
He's nearby. What?

260
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,260
Where is he?

261
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:48,597
There's really no point
at all in you asking that.

262
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:52,151
I, Whole Horse, will have the
pleasure of snuffing you out.

263
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,200
Arrogant morons like
you always talk trash.

264
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:59,049
and it always ends up
the other way around.

265
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,440
Oh, was that funny?

266
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,700
Lord Dio had you pegged.

267
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:07,657
Polnareff has the fatal habit of
underestimating his opponents.

268
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:10,657
Beating him into a corpse
won't be any trouble for you.

269
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:14,020
He was exactly right, so
I couldn't help but laugh.

270
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:20,629
If I can't face him until I defeat you,
then that's just what I'll do, chump.

271
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,600
Bring it on.

272
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,997
Ever heard of military chess?

273
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:29,657
The tank is stronger than the soldier,
and the tanks are weak against the mines.

274
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:32,269
See, it's pretty much
the basics of battle.

275
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:36,237
My emperor is stronger than you,
so I thought I'd be a gentleman.

276
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:40,555
I'll let you know my stand's abilities
before we fight, so we're square.

277
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,280
The gun is mightier than the sword.

278
00:18:44,100 --> 00:18:45,700
Such a brilliant quote.

279
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:49,140
What are you trying to say exactly?

280
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:54,117
That I have a stand that shoots,
and a sword simply can't beat that.

281
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,160
So what?

282
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,380
A pea-shooter?

283
00:19:08,620 --> 00:19:10,060
Prepare to die!

284
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:12,660
You underestimated me!

285
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:16,080
And now, Pawnareff, you're dead!

286
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:22,500
If I take off my armor, I
can knock down a bullet!

287
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:26,520
Wait, what the?

288
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,320
That's impossible!

289
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:31,180
It bypassed my sword! Oh, crap!

290
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:36,900
The bullet is also my stand, and
underestimating me just cost you your life.

291
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:43,990
Hold on!

292
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:51,600
What? Avdol?

293
00:19:52,300 --> 00:19:55,177
I've been worried about you,
and now look where you are!

294
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:57,420
Your ego will end you, Polnareff!

295
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:59,880
You're worried about me? Damn you!

296
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,977
You came here to lecture me again?

297
00:20:02,060 --> 00:20:04,437
The enemy already knows
everything about you!

298
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:08,814
You said you're a loner, but from now
on, you won't be able to win alone!

299
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:12,460
What bad timing for an
outsider to interfere.

300
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:16,337
Polnareff, move!

301
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,891
The bullet's coming back!

302
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:19,820
Go, Matrishit's Red!

303
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:23,160
All melted dough!

304
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:28,560
Damn that, Avdol!

305
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:30,722
He went after Polnareff himself!

306
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,500
Where are you, Mr. Avdol?

307
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,620
Polnareff, I have a terrible feeling.

308
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:43,145
Hey, there's a weird
fight going on over there!

309
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:57,840
The plot hole!

310
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:04,780
What the...

311
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:21,000
Mr. Avdol!

312
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:24,560
Man, today must be my day!

313
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:29,497
My gun and centerfold's mirror don't do
very well against Avdol's flames, you see.

314
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:32,345
We were sure he'd be our
most formidable enemy.

315
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,600
Talk about luck!

316
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:37,380
With him gone, the game is in the bag.

317
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:40,300
Mr. Avdol!

318
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,788
He's just hurt, that's all.

319
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:49,506
It's just a minor wound, see?

320
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:51,566
He's going to start speaking.

321
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,602
He'll open his eyes in a moment.

322
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:55,700
Right, Mr. Avdol? Right?

323
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:58,964
You're going to wake up, right?

324
00:21:59,160 --> 00:21:59,990
Mr.

325
00:22:00,073 --> 00:22:03,260
Avdol, you gotta wake up!
No, please! Mr. Avdol!

326
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:15,360
That seemed awfully easy.

327
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:18,500
It was too quick.

328
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:26,052
That's what he gets for lecturing people.

329
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:27,340
Look at him now.

330
00:22:28,100 --> 00:22:31,420
What did you say, Polnareff? Mr.

331
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:33,227
Avdol was worried about you.

332
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:36,129
Who asked him for help
because I never did?

333
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:38,897
He likes to meddle in
other people's business,

334
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:41,274
but he's slow as hell, so they got him.

335
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:44,557
Guys like him just get
in the way and screw up.

336
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:46,934
That's why I said I was going in alone.

337
00:22:47,540 --> 00:22:48,500
You bastard.

338
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:50,640
He saved your life.

339
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:51,940
How dare you?

340
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,200
I am sick of it!

341
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,600
Having people up and die on me!

342
00:23:13,140 --> 00:23:13,970
Polnareff...

343
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:18,440
I'm so sick of it!

344
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:21,480
You hear me?!

345
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:41,577
All the old paintings on the tomb?

346
00:23:41,660 --> 00:23:43,617
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

347
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:45,260
If they move too quick?

348
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:48,277
They're falling down like a domino!

349
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:50,937
All the birds are men by the Nile?

350
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:54,597
They've got their money on
a bed Called crocodiles!

351
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:57,577
They snap their teeth on your cigarette!

352
00:23:57,660 --> 00:23:59,920
Foreign types of the hookah! I say!

353
00:24:06,420 --> 00:24:08,800
Walk like an Egyptian!

354
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,177
The blonde waitresses!

355
00:24:22,260 --> 00:24:23,577
Take their trays!

356
00:24:23,660 --> 00:24:25,557
Spin around and they cross the floor!

357
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:27,077
They've got the moves!

358
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:29,017
You drop, you drink!

359
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:30,237
Then they bring you more!

360
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:32,857
All the school kids so sick of books!

361
00:24:32,940 --> 00:24:34,917
They like the punk and the metal band!

362
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:36,500
When the buzzer rings!

363
00:24:37,260 --> 00:24:39,177
They're walking like an Egyptian!

364
00:24:39,260 --> 00:24:42,597
All the kids in the marketplace say! Walk

365
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:49,680
like

366
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:50,810
an Egyptian!

367
00:24:53,820 --> 00:24:57,377
For such a tough guy, he
sure was easy to finish off?

368
00:24:57,460 --> 00:25:00,957
Come to think of it, that sweet sister
of yours was really good at sobbing.

369
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:03,437
You want me to hold these
regrets inside and run away?

370
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:04,437
Don't let him get to you.

371
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:05,697
You're much stronger than that.

372
00:25:05,780 --> 00:25:06,610
Mr.

373
00:25:06,693 --> 00:25:07,523
Avdol told you.

374
00:25:07,606 --> 00:25:08,861
He begged you not to fight alone.
